WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.960
Cell culture cannot show blood pressure or nervous-system wiring.

2
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:14.580
Before gene targeting, a mouse geneticist could add DNA at random, but could not

3
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.440
choose which gene to change.

4
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.100
So how do you test what one gene does in a whole animal?

5
00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:27.793
Embryonic stem cells, or ES cells, come from the early embryo and can still

6
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:29.273
contribute to any tissue.

7
00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:35.733
A targeting vector carries DNA matching the gene on both sides of the change: two

8
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:40.613
homology arms. Between them sits a neomycin resistance marker.

9
00:00:41.513 --> 00:00:44.253
Outside them sits a thymidine kinase marker.

10
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:47.173
Electroporation puts the vector in.

11
00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:53.873
In rare cells, homologous recombination swaps the vector's version into the gene's own place.

12
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:58.923
A drug, G418, kills cells with no vector.

13
00:00:59.743 --> 00:01:05.223
A correct swap loses the thymidine kinase gene, which lies outside the matching DNA.

14
00:01:06.163 --> 00:01:11.243
A random insertion keeps it, and thymidine kinase makes ganciclovir toxic.

15
00:01:12.783 --> 00:01:16.163
Survivors are screened by PCR or Southern blot, then expanded.

16
00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:23.017
ES cells are injected into blastocysts of a strain with a different coat colour, and

17
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:24.837
foster mothers carry the embryos.

18
00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:31.997
The pups are chimeras, part host and part ES cell, and coat colour shows the share.

19
00:01:33.157 --> 00:01:37.277
A chimera, usually male, is typically mated with a black strain.

20
00:01:38.357 --> 00:01:43.937
Agouti pups come from ES-derived germ cells, and tail DNA shows if they carry the

21
00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.957
allele. These are usually heterozygous.

22
00:01:47.737 --> 00:01:49.557
Further breeding gives homozygotes.

23
00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:56.887
At the cell stage, Koller and Smithies found two correct colonies among 234

24
00:01:56.887 --> 00:02:03.787
resistant ones. In mice, the phenotype is read by comparing homozygous null with

25
00:02:03.787 --> 00:02:10.247
wild-type. TrkA-null mice lose sympathetic neurons and many sensory neurons.

26
00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:15.927
Their superior cervical ganglion forms normally, then loses its neurons from

27
00:02:15.927 --> 00:02:18.047
embryonic day 15.5.

28
00:02:18.047 --> 00:02:20.867
Survival, not birth, failed.

29
00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:23.777
First, genetic background.

30
00:02:24.597 --> 00:02:30.477
The targeted gene is flanked by ES-cell DNA, which may carry its own mutations.

31
00:02:31.757 --> 00:02:36.917
Caspase-3-null mice on one strain died perinatally with exencephaly.

32
00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:41.577
On another strain they reached adulthood with minimal brain pathology.

33
00:02:42.337 --> 00:02:47.317
So backcross to a defined strain, and compare wild-type animals of the same

34
00:02:47.317 --> 00:02:50.397
background. Second, compensation.

35
00:02:51.677 --> 00:02:55.937
MyoD-null mice had normal muscle and raised Myf-5.

36
00:02:56.477 --> 00:02:58.437
So delete related genes together.

37
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:07.637
Bax-null mice, studied in 1995 and 1998 by Knudson and White with colleagues, had

38
00:03:07.637 --> 00:03:11.037
naturally occurring neuron death largely eliminated.

39
00:03:11.877 --> 00:03:14.277
A deletion in every cell could do that.

40
00:03:15.357 --> 00:03:23.237
In 2004, Glebova and Ginty combined Bax-null with NGF-null, so NGF's role in

41
00:03:23.237 --> 00:03:26.537
target innervation could be tested without neurons dying.

42
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:34.190
In 1997, Howell and colleagues deleted Dab1, and the brain copied the reeler brain.

43
00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.410
Reeler itself is a spontaneous mutant, not a knockout.

44
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:46.750
In 1999, Trommsdorff and colleagues removed both ApoER2 and VLDLR, and the

45
00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.370
phenotype mimicked reeler.

46
00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:52.230
Knock-ins change a gene instead of deleting it.

47
00:03:52.230 --> 00:04:00.430
In 2004, Fagiolini and colleagues put in a diazepam-insensitive alpha1 or alpha2 subunit.

48
00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:04.470
They found that alpha1 circuits drive the critical period.

49
00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.170
A knockout shows necessity, not sufficiency.
